<title>BELGIUM: Belgacom in security venture with Securis.</title>
<headline>Belgacom in security venture with Securis.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian state telephone company Belgacom said on Friday it expected 1,400 jobs to be created in the next six years through a joint security project with Belgian AviaPartner group unit Securis.</p>
<p>&quot;The agreement covers physical surveillance, monitoring and handling of alarms and of course intervention after alarm,&quot; it said in a satement.</p>
<p>The AviaPartner group operates in Europe in airport handling (Belgavia) and airport security (Securair). In Belgium it operates in the security sector through Securis.</p>
<p>Belgacom is 49 percent owned by a consortium comprising Ameritech, Singapore Telecom and Tele Danmark and three Belgian groups.</p>
<p>Belgacom's plan to move some of its staff to the new security joint venture forms part of plans to cut its costs in its core telephone business.</p>
